        "cited_text": "A more comprehensive suite of approaches falls under data-driven attribution (DDA) modeling. DDA models utilize machine learning and statistical techniques to allocate conversion credit. Methodologies such as Multi-Touch Attribution (MTA) and Marketing Mix Modeling (MMM), consider a broader range of factors and offer a more balanced view of the customer journey, from initial awareness to final conversion. MMM considers a top-down approach where channel touchpoints are modeled and account for seasonal and macroeconomic factors. MTA considers a bottom-up approach where member-level touchpoints are modeled and the touchpoint journey is captured."
